From: cezanne port
Subject: [PATCH] va: h264enc: take RGB input where the driver encodes RGB32

The cezanne VA driver (mainline/rootfs/libva-v4l2-request) lists
VA_RT_FORMAT_RGB32 for H.264 EncSlice: its encoder (cezanne-venc) reads
BGRx / RGBx dma-bufs and converts them to BT.709 itself. With RGB taken
here, GNOME's screen recorder (pipewiresrc DMA_DRM XR24 ! vapostproc !
vah264enc) runs vapostproc in passthrough and encodes the compositor's
buffers with no copy and no CPU conversion. Drivers without RGB32 for the
entrypoint fail the profile choice as before. The output caps get BT.709
colorimetry instead of the input's RGB one (mp4mux would otherwise tag
the stream GBR).

--- a/sys/va/gstvah264enc.c	2026-10-29 15:25:17.856668642 +0100
+++ b/sys/va/gstvah264enc.c	2026-10-29 15:28:24.678003568 +0100
@@ -1216,6 +1216,7 @@
     guint MbHeightC = 8;
 
     switch (base->rt_format) {
+      case VA_RT_FORMAT_RGB32:  /* coded as 8-bit 4:2:0 */
       case VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420:
         BitDepthY = 8;
         BitDepthC = 8;
@@ -1302,8 +1303,10 @@
 
   chroma = gst_va_chroma_from_video_format (format);
 
-  /* Check whether the rtformat is supported. */
-  if (chroma != VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420) {
+  /* Check whether the rtformat is supported. RGB is taken for drivers
+   * whose encoder converts it itself (the profile choice checks that the
+   * driver lists RGB32 for the entrypoint), saving a conversion pass. */
+  if (chroma != VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420 && chroma != VA_RT_FORMAT_RGB32) {
     GST_ERROR_OBJECT (self, "Unsupported chroma for video format: %s",
         gst_video_format_to_string (format));
     return 0;
@@ -1710,6 +1713,11 @@
 
   output_state =
       gst_video_encoder_set_output_state (venc, out_caps, base->input_state);
+  /* RGB input comes out as BT.709 limited range YCbCr (the driver's
+   * conversion), not with the RGB colorimetry of the input */
+  if (GST_VIDEO_INFO_IS_RGB (&base->in_info))
+    gst_video_colorimetry_from_string (&output_state->info.colorimetry,
+        GST_VIDEO_COLORIMETRY_BT709);
   gst_video_codec_state_unref (output_state);
 
   if (!gst_video_encoder_negotiate (venc)) {
